# Casos de Uso (Handlers Manuais)

## Estrutura por operação

Cada caso de uso é uma pasta com 4 arquivos:

```
Application/Product/Commands/CreateProduct/
  CreateProductCommand.cs
  ICreateProductHandler.cs
  CreateProductHandler.cs
  CreateProductValidator.cs
```

## Contratos

```csharp
public sealed record CreateProductCommand(string Name, decimal Price);

public interface ICreateProductHandler
{
    Task<ProductResponse> HandleAsync(CreateProductCommand command, CancellationToken ct);
}
```

## Handler

```csharp
public sealed class CreateProductHandler(
    IProductDomainService productDomainService,
    IUnitOfWork unitOfWork,
    CreateProductValidator validator) : ICreateProductHandler
{
    public async Task<ProductResponse> HandleAsync(CreateProductCommand command, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        await validator.ValidateAndThrowAsync(command, ct);
        var product = await productDomainService.CreateAsync(command.Name, command.Price, ct);
        await unitOfWork.SaveChangesAsync(ct);
        return ProductResponse.From(product);
    }
}
```

Application **nunca** injeta `I*Repository`. Persistência passa pelo Domain Service; o Handler só orquestra e commita via `IUnitOfWork`.

## Registro DI

Registrar cada handler em `Application/DependencyInjection/DependencyInjection.cs`:

```csharp
services.AddScoped<ICreateProductHandler, CreateProductHandler>();
```

## Queries

Mesmo padrão: `GetProductQuery` + `IGetProductHandler` + `GetProductHandler`.
